IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia71-types`

-- Immigration Act 1971 (UK) — GOALS 1 AND 2: RIGHT OF ABODE, NEED FOR LEAVE,
-- AND CONTINUATION OF LEAVE (ss 1-3, 3C, 3ZA).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1971-77.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — right of abode and the need for leave`

-- s 2(1) "A person is ... to have the right of abode in the United Kingdom
-- if— (a) he is a British citizen; or (b) he is a Commonwealth citizen who—
-- (i) immediately before the commencement of the British Nationality Act
-- 1981 was a Commonwealth citizen having the right of abode ...; and (ii) has
-- not ceased to be a Commonwealth citizen in the meanwhile."
@ref s 2(1)
@export Whether a person has the right of abode in the United Kingdom under s 2 of the Immigration Act 1971 (UK): a British citizen, or a Commonwealth citizen who had the right of abode immediately before the British Nationality Act 1981 commenced and has remained a Commonwealth citizen. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Person facts`  @desc Citizenship, and the pre-1983 Commonwealth right of abode
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the right of abode` p IF
        p's `a British citizen`
    OR  (p's `a Commonwealth citizen with the right of abode before 1983` AND p's `still a Commonwealth citizen`)

-- s 1(1)-(2): those with the right of abode are free to come and go; others
-- need permission. s 3ZA(1): "An Irish citizen does not require leave ...
-- unless subsection (2), (3) or (4) applies". s 1(3): no leave is needed on
-- a local journey within the common travel area — but (s 3ZA(5)) not for an
-- Irish citizen within (2)-(4).
@ref ss 1(1)-(3), 3(1), 3ZA
@export Whether a person requires leave to enter the United Kingdom under the Immigration Act 1971 (UK): not if they have the right of abode, are an Irish citizen not deported or excluded (s 3ZA), or arrive on a local journey within the common travel area (s 1(3)) — except an Irish citizen who is deported or excluded; otherwise they do. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Person facts`  @desc Citizenship, any deportation or exclusion, and whether they arrive on a local journey
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `requires leave to enter` p IF
        NOT (`has the right of abode` p)
    AND NOT irishFree
    AND NOT (p's `arriving on a local journey within the common travel area` AND NOT excludedIrish)
    WHERE
        excludedIrish MEANS p's `an Irish citizen` AND p's `deported, excluded by directions, or excluded under s 8B`
        irishFree MEANS p's `an Irish citizen` AND NOT (p's `deported, excluded by directions, or excluded under s 8B`)

§ `Goal 2 — continuation of leave (s 3C)`

-- s 3C(1): "(a) a person who has limited leave ... applies ... for variation
-- of the leave, (b) the application for variation is made before the leave
-- expires, and (c) the leave expires without the application ... having been
-- decided." (2): the leave is extended during any period when the
-- application is undecided, or an in-country appeal or administrative review
-- could be brought or is pending. (3): it lapses if the applicant leaves.
@ref s 3C(1)-(3)
@export Whether a person's limited leave is extended under s 3C of the Immigration Act 1971 (UK) on a given day after it would have expired: the application to vary was made on or before the expiry day and had not been decided by then, and on that day the application is still undecided or an in-country appeal or administrative review could still be brought or is pending; not on or after the day the applicant left the United Kingdom. On or before the expiry day the leave runs anyway. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Leave extension facts`  @desc The expiry, application, decision and appeal dates, and any departure
      d IS A DATE                     @desc The day in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the leave is extended by s 3C under` f `on` d IF
        d GREATER THAN f's `leave expires on`
    AND f's `application made on` AT MOST f's `leave expires on`
    AND undecidedAtExpiry
    AND (undecidedOn OR rightsRunning)
    AND notLeft
    WHERE
        undecidedAtExpiry MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `decided or withdrawn on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST x  THEN x GREATER THAN f's `leave expires on`
        undecidedOn MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `decided or withdrawn on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST x  THEN d LESS THAN x
        rightsRunning MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `appeal or review rights end on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST x  THEN d AT MOST x
        notLeft MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `left the United Kingdom on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST x  THEN d LESS THAN x
